From 4d28e047a7356fece231c5f49ae6ee5fee6b67f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:37:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] checkpoints: apply the size cap before git add;
 clean up and back off after a staging timeout

A project holding one multi-GB file (database, dataset, weights) made every
checkpoint run `git add -A` past its timeout: the "skip files over
max_file_size_mb" rule ran only after staging (_drop_oversize_from_index),
when git had already hashed and compressed the file. The snapshot was lost,
the killed git left a partial tmp_pack (hundreds of MB) and the project
index lock in the store (so every later checkpoint of that folder failed on
the lock), and the folder was retried, and waited on, every turn.

- tools/checkpoint_staging.py (new sibling): one tree walk (replaces
  _dir_file_count) counts entries and collects files over the cap plus the
  3 biggest files; a per-project core.excludesFile of anchored literal
  gitignore patterns; timeout debris cleanup (tmp_pack_*/tmp_obj_*/index
  lock written since the call started; callers hold the store lock); a
  per-process 1 h back-off registry.
- CheckpointManager._stage_all: git add -A with the oversize excludes, after
  unstaging those paths (excludes do not apply to tracked entries, e.g. a
  file that grew past the cap). Used by _take, _diff and _safe_restore_plan
  (which still lists oversize files as changed, as before).
- _unstage uses update-index --force-remove: literal paths, and it does not
  refuse an entry whose staged content differs from file and ref.
- A staging timeout logs the working folder (git timeout message) and its 3
  biggest files, and the folder is skipped for 60 min.
- _drop_oversize_from_index stays as the backstop.

Tests (tests/tools/test_checkpoint_manager.py), all red on the base:
TestOversizeFilesNeverStaged (50 MB file under a 1 MB cap never reaches the
store; a file that grew past the cap is unstaged first) and
TestGitTimeoutRecovery (partial pack, loose temp and index lock removed,
older foreign debris kept, next turn and other managers skip git add until
the window ends; the log names the folder and biggest files).
